--- SUMMARY ---

# Final User Stories — CLI Calculator MVP

**Language:** Python | **Input style:** Token-by-token, one value per Enter | **No external libraries**

---

| # | Title | Description | Effort |
|---|-------|-------------|--------|
| US1 | Basic input loop | Bootstrap the app. Display `0` on start. Accept input from the user in a loop, echo it back. No logic yet — just the skeleton that all other stories build on. | Low |
| US2 | Multi-digit number input | User types an integer (one or more digits 0–9). Display updates to show the full number. Single-digit input is a subset of this — no need for a separate story. | Low |
| US3 | Operator input | User types `+`, `-`, `*`, or `/` after a number. App stores the operator and the current number, then waits for the next number. Typing an operator in any invalid position (e.g. no number yet, or after another operator) displays `Error`. | Medium |
| US4 | Equals command | User types `=`. App evaluates the pending operation left-to-right using the stored number, operator, and current input. Displays the result. No `eval()` — implement arithmetic explicitly. | Medium |
| US5 | Error handling | Catches: operator after operator, division by zero, invalid tokens (anything not a digit, operator, `=`, `c`, or `exit`), empty operator (e.g. `=` with no full expression). Displays `Error`. Next valid input resets state cleanly. | Medium |
| US6 | Clear command | User types `c`. Resets all state (current number, pending operator, pending result) back to initial. Display returns to `0`. Works from any state including error. | Low |
| US7 | Exit command | User types `exit`. Loop terminates cleanly. No error thrown, no hanging process. | Low |

---

**Decisions captured for implementers:**
- Empty Enter → no-op, re-display current value
- Leading zeros (e.g. `007`) → valid, parse as integer normally
- Chained operations evaluate left-to-right, no precedence
- Division by zero → `Error`, reset on next input
